# Netlify reads this file at deploy time and applies these as real HTTP
# response headers. There is no meta-tag equivalent for X-Frame-Options or
# X-Content-Type-Options — both are ignored by browsers unless set here (see
# docs/audit-1.0.2.md, finding on this). Vercel uses vercel.json instead;
# GitHub Pages supports neither, since it serves static files with no custom
# response-header mechanism.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
